      "description": "Navy header with air-mail stripe edge and the ES/EN toggle.",
      "html": "<header class=\"ds-shell\"><div class=\"ds-bar\"><strong>Buzón de webhooks</strong><div class=\"ds-lang\"><button aria-pressed=\"true\">ES</button><button>EN</button></div></div></header>",
      "css": ".ds-shell{background:#15254a;color:#eef3fc;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-shell::after{content:\"\";display:block;height:6px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,#c8102e 0 14px,#fff 14px 20px,#1f4fa3 20px 34px,#fff 34px 40px)}.ds-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;min-height:64px;padding:0 20px;font-size:18px;font-weight:650}.ds-lang{display:flex;padding:2px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16)}.ds-lang button{height:28px;min-width:36px;border:0;border-radius:6px;background:transparent;color:#aebbd6;font:650 12px system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;cursor:pointer}.ds-lang button:hover{color:#eef3fc}.ds-lang button[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:#eef3fc;color:#15254a}.ds-lang button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #fff;outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Postmark",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "status-chip-ok",
      "description": "Signature per-delivery cancellation mark in state ink; stamps in once.",
      "html": "<svg class=\"ds-pm\" viewBox=\"0 0 112 74\"><defs><path id=\"ds-t\" d=\"M 9.5 37 A 27.5 27.5 0 0 1 64.5 37\"/><path id=\"ds-b\" d=\"M 8 41 A 29 29 0 0 0 66 41\"/></defs><g transform=\"rotate(-4 37 37)\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"><circle cx=\"37\" cy=\"37\" r=\"33\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><circle cx=\"37\" cy=\"37\" r=\"21\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text font-size=\"8.2\" font-weight=\"700\" letter-spacing=\"1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"><textPath href=\"#ds-t\" startOffset=\"50%\">19 NOV 2026</textPath></text><text font-size=\"8.2\" font-weight=\"700\" letter-spacing=\"1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"><textPath href=\"#ds-b\" startOffset=\"50%\">11:01:56</textPath></text><text x=\"37\" y=\"42.5\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">200</text></g><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\".85\"><path d=\"M74 25 q4.5 -4 9 0 t9 0 t9 0 t9 0\"/><path d=\"M74 37 q4.5 -4 9 0 t9 0 t9 0 t9 0\"/><path d=\"M74 49 q4.5 -4 9 0 t9 0 t9 0 t9 0\"/></g></svg>",
      "css": ".ds-pm{width:112px;height:74px;color:var(--ok,#1b7343);font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;overflow:visible}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.ds-pm{animation:ds-stamp .22s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1) both}}@keyframes ds-stamp{from{transform:scale(1.35);opacity:0}to{transform:scale(1);opacity:1}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Signature Header Row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "signature-ink",
      "description": "Headers tile rows; signature headers sort first with an air-blue wash.",
      "html": "<dl class=\"ds-h\"><div class=\"ds-row ds-sig\"><dt>stripe-signature</dt><dd>t=1731990000,v1=5f1c9a0b7e3d42c8</dd></div><div class=\"ds-row\"><dt>content-type</dt><dd>application/json</dd></div></dl>",
      "css": ".ds-h{margin:0;display:grid}.ds-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(140px,220px) minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;padding:7px 8px;border-radius:6px}.ds-row+.ds-row{border-top:1px dashed var(--line,#d2dbe7)}.ds-row dt{font:600 12.5px ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;color:var(--ink-2,#4b5b78)}.ds-row dd{margin:0;font:12.5px/1.5 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;word-break:break-all}.ds-sig{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--air-blue,#1f4fa3) 9%,transparent)}.ds-sig dt{color:var(--sig-ink,#1f4fa3)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Air-Mail Sorting Table",
    "overview": "Every delivery is a letter laid on a sorting table and cancelled with a postmark that states when it arrived and what the endpoint answered. The chrome is an air-mail envelope: a navy shell band edged with a red/white/blue chevron stripe, sitting over cool paper (light) or night navy (dark). Content lives on white sheets with a thin rule and a soft ambient lift.\n\nThe system is quiet and dense, built for a page that sits beside the editor and is glanced at, not studied. Color is rationed: the air-mail red and blue belong to the envelope edge and the signature header; everywhere else, ink colors carry state only, green for 2xx and red for 4xx or invalid. System sans runs the interface; monospace is reserved for what came over the wire (payloads, headers, URLs, status codes, times).\n\nLight and dark are both first-class and follow the OS (`prefers-color-scheme`). Every token below has a dark counterpart in the sidecar; the dark world is night navy ground, raised navy sheets, and lifted pastel inks, not an inversion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy shell band with a 6px diagonal air-mail stripe as its lower edge.",
      "White sheets on cool paper, 10px corners, 1px rule, two-layer ambient shadow.",
      "Status is spoken in ink color plus a mono code chip, never color alone.",
      "One circular postmark per delivery, slightly rotated, stamped in once on arrival.",
      "Monospace only for wire data; tabular numerals everywhere."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State Ink Rule",
        "body": "Green and red mean HTTP outcome and nothing else. They never decorate, and they always travel with a printed code (200, 400, INVÁLIDO) so color is never the only signal.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Envelope Edge Rule",
        "body": "Air-mail red and blue appear only on the shell stripe and identity marks. Spreading them into content turns the envelope into a flag.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wire Is Mono Rule",
        "body": "If it came over HTTP or will be pasted into a terminal, it is set in monospace; UI copy never is.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Lift Rule",
        "body": "Only sheets and the toast cast shadows. Rows, fields, and code blocks separate by border and tone.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do route every color through the custom properties so light and dark stay paired.",
      "Do pair each state ink with a printed code or label (The State Ink Rule).",
      "Do set wire data (payloads, headers, URLs, codes, times) in the mono stack, with tabular numerals.",
      "Do keep one filled primary button per screen; everything else is quiet.",
      "Do keep motion to state feedback (150-200ms) plus the single 220ms stamp-in, and honor `prefers-reduced-motion`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use air-mail red or blue as content accents; they belong to the envelope edge (The Envelope Edge Rule).",
      "Don't use green or red for anything but HTTP outcome.",
      "Don't add shadows to rows, fields, or code blocks (The One Lift Rule).",
      "Don't render deliveries as a grid of identical JSON cards; each one is a list row with its postmark."
    ]
  }
}
